Statement of changes (Apache License, Version 2.0, Section 4(b))
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following areas were added or modified by the SALMON-TROUT contributors
relative to upstream SALMON (branch develop-2.0.0). The authoritative record
of every change is the project's git history.

  * src/ssbe/ - a velocity-gauge semiconductor Bloch equation (SBE) solver
    extended with many-body CPTP Lindblad dissipation (electron-phonon,
    impact ionization, Auger, carrier-carrier thermalization, graphene 2D
    Rana Auger/carrier-multiplication) and a nonlocal, momentum-conserving
    "ring" super-mode for intervalley transfer.

  * src/epm/ and the top-level epm_*.py builders - an empirical
    pseudopotential (EPM) band-structure front end (Si, GaAs, CdS,
    graphene; folded supercells and non-orthogonal primitive cells) that
    feeds the SBE.

  * Top-level Python tools - plot_sbe_results.py, plot_tddft_results.py,
    si_three_photon_isosurfaces.py, zener_tunneling_estimate.py,
    band_field_coupling.py and related analysis/visualization scripts.

  * samples/exercise_x*/ - runnable EPM->SBE example input decks.

  * wiki/ and README.md - fork documentation, including the master-equation
    reference.

  * tests/ - added Fortran and Python unit tests for the above.

  * Integration hooks in pre-existing SALMON driver and I/O sources
    (e.g. src/io/, src/rt/, src/main.f90). These modified upstream files
    carry both their original SALMON copyright notice and, by reference,
    this statement of modification.

